This is the workaround I see for v1:

```js
search.addWidget(
  instantsearch.widgets.refinementList({
    container: '#brand-list',
    attributeName: 'brand',
    // v2 version:
    // transformItems: items => items.filter(item => item.label !== 'Sony'),
    transformData: {
      item(item) {
        if (item.name === 'Sony') {
          // uses a bug in InstantSearch v1,
          // which will not add the classes on empty items
          return {};
        }
        return item;
      },
    },
  })
);
```

Then you can hide it with css:

```css
.ais-refinement-list--item label:not(.ais-refinement-list--label) {
  display: none;
}
```

